// A hand-written GIFT file covering every question type the format carries.
$CATEGORY: science/review

// true/false, with general feedback
::TF1:: Water boils at 100 °C at sea level. {TRUE ####At sea level, yes.}

// multiple choice
::MC1:: Which gas do plants take in? { =carbon dioxide ~oxygen ~nitrogen }

// a missing word, with several accepted answers
::FB1:: A spider has {=eight =8} legs.

// short answer: accepted answers and no wrong ones, after the text
::SA1:: Which planet is called the red planet? { =Mars =the red planet }

// matching
::MA1:: Match each animal with its food. { =cat -> fish =cow -> grass =bird -> seeds }

// numeric with a tolerance, and a range
::NU1:: How many days are in a leap year? {#366:0}

::NU2:: Name a number from 1 to 5. {#1..5}

// essay
::ES1:: Explain how a rainbow forms. {}

// multiple answer: weights with no single right answer
::MU1:: Which of these are mammals? { ~%50%whale ~%50%bat ~%-100%shark }

// escapes
::ES2:: Which answer equals 5? { ~\= 2 + 2 =\= 2 + 3 ~\= 2 + 4 }

// a picture GIFT cannot carry
::PI1:: [html]<p>What is shown?</p><img src="cell.png" alt="a cell"> { =a plant cell ~an animal cell }

// a description, text between questions
::Intro:: The next question is about space.

$CATEGORY: space
::SP1:: The Moon orbits the Earth. {T}
